// DEMO: the keeper seat (`demo=keeper`, `src/lab/demo/keeper.rs`). The
// player is a hand over the box, not an ant: they sketch galleries, and
// teach the colony a far station by carrying an ant there or treating it.
//
// The nest goal's box (no plants, mister off) with the colony landed at
// once at the west end (x: 107, `far_larder`'s measured column: the
// smallest at which all 52 land) on a founding heap. The far station
// (column 390 by default, ~180 columns past the colony band's east edge)
// and the ration inside the nest are kept by `keeper.rs`, not by this file,
// because a top-up reads the box: the timeline cannot say "back up to 80".
//
// **Stakes (2026-10-30, on by default; `stakes=0` is the box above):** no
// station and no top-up. `keeper.rs` drops windfalls at seeded random far
// columns that rot to ash, cuts the nest ration once the round opens, and
// runs the round, the hand's charges and the verdict card. They are not
// timeline events because each reads the box (a seeded column clear of the
// live windfalls, the cells left on one when it rots).
(
    name: "demo_keeper",
    title: "DEMO: THE KEEPER",
    question: "Can a hand that carries and feeds ants teach a trained colony where far food is -- and does the lesson spread mouth to mouth and fade if you stop?",
    bed: (
        width: 512,
        height: 320,
        soil_depth: 80,
        ground_y: 160,
        compartments: 1,
        founders: 0,
        species: "grass",
        colonies: 0,
        colony_ants: 52,
        colony_species: "ant",
        predators: 0,
        lamp_spacing: 33,
        seed: 1,
        extra_walls: [],
    ),
    settings: [
        (subject: "the bed", field: "rain", value: 0),
    ],
    placements: [
        Colony(species: "ant", x: 107, count: 52),
        Heap(material: "provisions", x: 137, cells: 120),
    ],
    timeline: [],
    horizon: 36000,
)
